line 49, 50 type: bug SUB-1546 `x` in `x++` after a `typeof` guard is recorded with its declared type (here a literal-typed parameter, which `++` widens to `number` per spec §1.3)
line 112 type: by-design spec §1.6 `a && b` is `falsy_part(a) | b`, even when `a` is always falsy
line 115 type: by-design spec §1.6 the result of `||` or `??` includes the right operand's type, even when the left can't fall through to it
